{
    "id": "897f48f8-9e93-4b03-89e9-8d87434677cc",
    "companyId": "87c32b8e-f131-4df8-ad8e-963d01b458e7",
    "projectId": null,
    "projectWorkspaceId": null,
    "goalId": "6eace62f-8d6f-4543-b419-75d98c7da6e9",
    "parentId": "bab4bab3-d4e5-4f2b-922c-50f02fdd2715",
    "title": "Corrected parallel-session soak harness (scheduler-driven, functional low-cost agent)",
    "description": "Corrected, authorization-clean harness for the JAC-3269 parallel-session soak. Supersedes the literal JAC-3269 steps 2\u20135, which assume a capability the implemented control plane deliberately forbids.\n\n## Why the original steps 2\u20135 cannot run as written\n- **Session create/wake is self-scoped.** `POST /api/agents/{id}/sessions` and `.../sessions/{id}/wake` return `403 {\"error\":\"Agent can only manage its own sessions\"}` for any agent token targeting a *different* agent. A worker agent (Herald) structurally cannot drive another agent's sessions. Confirmed live 2026-08-01.\n- **`_test_probe` is not a functional target.** adapter=`process`, `adapterConfig={}`; every historical `heartbeat-run` is `status:failed`. It can never produce 3 concurrent *running* heartbeats or accrue budget.\n- Running the soak from inside a live heartbeat of the executing agent is exactly what JAC-3269 forbids.\n\n## What IS already proven (recorded on JAC-3269)\n- Step 1 `runtimeConfig.maxConcurrentSessions=3` PATCH \u2192 **HTTP 200** (prior `agents:create` 403 is resolved).\n- `heartbeat-runs` schema carries `sessionId`, `sessionIdBefore`, `sessionIdAfter`, `usageJson`, `wakeupRequestId` \u2014 the data path for \"distinct session_id per run\" and per-agent budget rollup exists.\n- Checkout mutual-exclusion returns **409** under contention (verified via active-hold conflict).\n\n## Corrected executable procedure (scheduler-driven, no self-scoped wake)\n1. Provision a **functional low-cost throwaway agent** (e.g. `claude_local`/haiku or `hermes_local` deepseek-flash). Do NOT reuse `_test_probe`. Set `runtimeConfig.heartbeat.enabled=true`, `heartbeat.maxConcurrentRuns=3`, `maxConcurrentSessions=3`.\n2. Create **3 trivial ready issues** (todo) assigned to that agent \u2014 each a no-op/\"acknowledge and close\" task. Distinct issues so each checks out to a different run.\n3. Let the **scheduler** spawn the concurrent runs (this is the legitimate wake path; no self-scoped `/wake` call needed).\n4. `GET /api/companies/{companyId}/heartbeat-runs?agentId=...` \u2192 assert \u22653 runs with **distinct `sessionId`**, `status:running`, and **overlapping** `startedAt`/`finishedAt` windows. (Step 3)\n5. Assert a second run cannot check out an issue already held by another run \u2192 **409**. (Step 4)\n6. Snapshot `agent.spentMonthlyCents` before/after and sum `usageJson` across the 3 runs; assert the per-agent total aggregates all sessions. (Step 5)\n7. **Cleanup:** `heartbeat.enabled=false`, `maxConcurrentSessions=1`, cancel/close the 3 test issues, pause or delete the throwaway agent. (Step 6)\n\n## Design-gap feedback for Phase 3 owner (JAC-3268)\nJAC-3269's acceptance criteria reference `POST /api/agents/{id}/sessions` + `.../wake` as the concurrency trigger, but those routes are self-scoped and cannot be used cross-agent. The acceptance criteria should be restated in terms of the scheduler-driven path above, or a privileged operator/board-user session-driver endpoint must be documented if manual cross-agent wake is intended to be testable.\n\nOwner: Herald. Continuation: JAC-3269 auto-wakes when this closes (first-class blocker).\n",
