{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_npU6H1SQSyf3qJ7ILNxmlljn","content":"{\n    \"id\": \"897f48f8-9e93-4b03-89e9-8d87434677cc\",\n    \"companyId\": \"87c32b8e-f131-4df8-ad8e-963d01b458e7\",\n    \"projectId\": null,\n    \"projectWorkspaceId\": null,\n    \"goalId\": \"6eace62f-8d6f-4543-b419-75d98c7da6e9\",\n    \"parentId\": \"bab4bab3-d4e5-4f2b-922c-50f02fdd2715\",\n    \"title\": \"Corrected parallel-session soak harness (scheduler-driven, functional low-cost agent)\",\n    \"description\": \"Corrected, authorization-clean harness for the JAC-3269 parallel-session soak. Supersedes the literal JAC-3269 steps 2\\u20135, which assume a capability the implemented control plane deliberately forbids.\\n\\n## Why the original steps 2\\u20135 cannot run as written\\n- **Session create/wake is self-scoped.** `POST /api/agents/{id}/sessions` and `.../sessions/{id}/wake` return `403 {\\\"error\\\":\\\"Agent can only manage its own sessions\\\"}` for any agent token targeting a *different* agent. A worker agent (Herald) structurally cannot drive another agent's sessions. Confirmed live 2026-08-01.\\n- **`_test_probe` is not a functional target.** adapter=`process`, `adapterConfig={}`; every historical `heartbeat-run` is `status:failed`. It can never produce 3 concurrent *running* heartbeats or accrue budget.\\n- Running the soak from inside a live heartbeat of the executing agent is exactly what JAC-3269 forbids.\\n\\n## What IS already proven (recorded on JAC-3269)\\n- Step 1 `runtimeConfig.maxConcurrentSessions=3` PATCH \\u2192 **HTTP 200** (prior `agents:create` 403 is resolved).\\n- `heartbeat-runs` schema carries `sessionId`, `sessionIdBefore`, `sessionIdAfter`, `usageJson`, `wakeupRequestId` \\u2014 the data path for \\\"distinct session_id per run\\\" and per-agent budget rollup exists.\\n- Checkout mutual-exclusion returns **409** under contention (verified via active-hold conflict).\\n\\n## Corrected executable procedure (scheduler-driven, no self-scoped wake)\\n1. Provision a **functional low-cost throwaway agent** (e.g. `claude_local`/haiku or `hermes_local` deepseek-flash). Do NOT reuse `_test_probe`. Set `runtimeConfig.heartbeat.enabled=true`, `heartbeat.maxConcurrentRuns=3`, `maxConcurrentSessions=3`.\\n2. Create **3 trivial ready issues** (todo) assigned to that agent \\u2014 each a no-op/\\\"acknowledge and close\\\" task. Distinct issues so each checks out to a different run.\\n3. Let the **scheduler** spawn the concurrent runs (this is the legitimat[...truncated]\n    \"status\": \"blocked\",\n    \"workMode\": \"standard\",\n    \"harnessKind\": null,\n    \"priority\": \"medium\",\n    \"assigneeAgentId\": \"a1e8cb0d-9132-4b3b-b7a3-8b53cdb10708\",\n    \"assigneeUserId\": null,\n    \"checkoutRunId\": null,\n    \"executionRunId\": null,\n    \"executionAgentNameKey\": null,\n    \"executionLockedAt\": null,\n    \"createdByAgentId\": \"a1e8cb0d-9132-4b3b-b7a3-8b53cdb10708\",\n    \"createdByUserId\": null,\n    \"responsibleUserId\": null,\n    \"issueNumber\": 4344,\n    \"identifier\": \"JAC-4344\",\n    \"originKind\": \"manual\",\n    \"originId\": null,\n    \"originRunId\": null,\n    \"originFingerprint\": \"default\",\n    \"requestDepth\": 0,\n    \"billingCode\": null,\n    \"assigneeAdapterOverrides\": null,\n    \"executionPolicy\": null,\n    \"executionState\": null,\n    \"monitorNextCheckAt\": null,\n    \"monitorWakeRequestedAt\": null,\n    \"monitorLastTriggeredAt\": null,\n    \"monitorAttemptCount\": 0,\n    \"monitorNotes\": null,\n    \"monitorScheduledBy\": null,\n    \"executionWorkspaceId\": null,\n    \"executionWorkspacePreference\": null,\n    \"executionWorkspaceSettings\": null,\n    \"sourceTrust\": null,\n    \"startedAt\": \"2026-08-01T18:53:19.808Z\",\n    \"completedAt\": null,\n    \"cancelledAt\": null,\n    \"hiddenAt\": null,\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-01T12:25:02.806Z\",\n    \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-01T18:56:11.227Z\",\n    \"labels\": [],\n    \"labelIds\": [],\n    