    "description": "First-class blocker for **JAC-4344** (and transitively JAC-3269). Created by Herald to stop the re-dispatch loop: JAC-4344 kept flipping back to `in_progress` on checkout with no blocker edge, so the scheduler re-woke it every cycle even though the work is not agent-executable.\n\n## Why this exists (verified live 2026-08-01, Herald run)\n\nThe corrected scheduler-driven soak is authorization-clean but **cannot be run or observed by any worker-agent token**. Two operator-owned capabilities are missing:\n\n1. **No agent-readable run-observability endpoint.** `GET .../heartbeat-runs` (company-, agent-, bare-scoped), `/runs`, `/agent-runs`, `/agents/{id}/sessions`, `/heartbeats` \u2014 **all 8 forms return HTTP 404**. Soak Steps 4 & 6 (distinct `sessionId`, overlapping windows, `usageJson` rollup) are structurally unobservable from the agent API even though the columns exist in-schema.\n2. **No provisionable execution lane.** `heartbeat.enabled=true` on an agent record does not create a physical runner. 44/46 fleet agents have heartbeat off; the one enabled agent (Luna) has no verified `executionLane`. A throwaway agent would spawn 0 running heartbeats. Binding a real runner is host-side infra (omnigent/OpenClaw/claude-code), not an agent-accessible mutation.\n\n## Owner decision required (three paths \u2014 see the `ask_user_questions` interaction on JAC-4344, id `jac4344:soak-unblock-decision:v1`)\n\n* **A \u2014 Operator runs the soak host-side:** run the 3-run concurrency soak directly against the DB/host where `heartbeat_runs` + `usageJson` are readable; paste the receipt. Closes JAC-3269/4344.\n* **B \u2014 Provision runner + expose read endpoint, then re-dispatch:** operator provisions a functional low-cost throwaway agent bound to a real lane AND exposes an agent-readable `GET heartbeat-runs`; re-dispatch JAC-4344 to Herald to run the full assert/cleanup harness.\n* **C \u2014 Restate acceptance (JAC-3268 owner Fable):** accept Phase-3 concurrency as already code-live + unit-verified, with primitives confirmed (maxConcurrentSessions PATCH 200; checkout 409; per-agent budget counter; session/usage schema). Restate JAC-3269 acceptance to the scheduler/code-verified path; close JAC-3269/4344 as satisfied.\n\n## Liveness / continuation\n\nThis issue is `blocked` on a board/operator decision \u2014 the live surface is the JAC-4344 interaction (continuationPolicy `wake_assignee`, wakes Herald on answer). Wings: route to the board/operator or action a path directly. When a path is chosen, close this issue \u2192 JAC-4344 unblocks \u2192 JAC-3269 auto-wakes.\n\nOwner: Wings (route/execute). Requester: Herald.",
