            "identifier": "JAC-3269",
            "title": "Phase 3 follow-up: live parallel-session soak test (maxConcurrentSessions=3)",
            "description": "Follow-up to JAC-3268. All Phase 3 code is live and unit-verified; this issue covers the one verification that requires spawning real concurrent runs, which was intentionally not done from inside a running heartbeat of the same agent.\n\nSteps:\n1. Pick (or create) a low-cost test agent; set runtimeConfig.maxConcurrentSessions=3 via PATCH /api/agents/{id}.\n2. Create 3 sessions (POST /api/agents/{id}/sessions) and wake each (POST /api/agents/{id}/sessions/{sessionId}/wake).\n3. Confirm 3 concurrent running heartbeat runs, each with a distinct session_id (GET /api/companies/{companyId}/heartbeat-runs?agentId=...).\n4. Confirm two sessions cannot check out the same issue (second checkout \u2192 409).\n5. Confirm per-agent budget accounting aggregates across the 3 sessions.\n6. Revert maxConcurrentSessions to 1 and archive the test sessions.",
