es/.hermes/logs/qwen-prewarm-telemetry.jsonl.\",\n        \"level\": \"company\",\n        \"status\": \"active\",\n        \"parentId\": null,\n        \"ownerAgentId\": \"0b902be0-2365-4599-b86d-bf177caf5550\",\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-07-10T17:04:04.420Z\",\n        \"updatedAt\": \"2026-07-15T02:11:16.858Z\"\n    },\n    \"mentionedProjects\": [],\n    \"currentExecutionWorkspace\": null,\n    \"workProducts\": [],\n    \"linkedCases\": []\n}\n\n=== JAC-4390 ===\n{\n    \"id\": \"bd21d0da-a291-46c9-ba0f-a3ed7fdc9678\",\n    \"companyId\": \"87c32b8e-f131-4df8-ad8e-963d01b458e7\",\n    \"projectId\": null,\n    \"projectWorkspaceId\": null,\n    \"goalId\": \"6eace62f-8d6f-4543-b419-75d98c7da6e9\",\n    \"parentId\": \"bab4bab3-d4e5-4f2b-922c-50f02fdd2715\",\n    \"title\": \"Board/operator gate: enable OR restate acceptance for JAC-3269 parallel-session soak\",\n    \"description\": \"First-class blocker for **JAC-4344** (and transitively JAC-3269). Created by Herald to stop the re-dispatch loop: JAC-4344 kept flipping back to `in_progress` on checkout with no blocker edge, so the scheduler re-woke it every cycle even though the work is not agent-executable.\\n\\n## Why this exists (verified live 2026-08-01, Herald run)\\n\\nThe corrected scheduler-driven soak is authorization-clean but **cannot be run or observed by any worker-agent token**. Two operator-owned capabilities are missing:\\n\\n1. **No agent-readable run-observability endpoint.** `GET .../heartbeat-runs` (company-, agent-, bare-scoped), `/runs`, `/agent-runs`, `/agents/{id}/sessions`, `/heartbeats` \\u2014 **all 8 forms return HTTP 404**. Soak Steps 4 & 6 (distinct `sessionId`, overlapping windows, `usageJson` rollup) are structurally unobservable from the agent API even though the columns exist in-schema.\\n2. **No provisionable execution lane.** `heartbeat.enabled=true` on an agent record does not create a physical runner. 44/46 fleet agents have heartbeat off; the one enabled agent (Luna) has no verified `executionLane`. A throwaway agent would spawn 0 running heartbeats. Binding a real runner is host-side infra (omnigent/OpenClaw/claude-code), not an agent-accessible mutation.\\n\\n## Owner decision required (three paths \\u2014 see the `ask_user_questions` interaction on JAC-4344, id `jac4344:soak-unblock-decision:v1`)\\n\\n* **A \\u2014 Operator runs the soak host-side:** run the 3-run concurrency soak directly against the DB/host where `heartbeat_runs` + `usageJson` are readable; paste the receipt. Closes JAC-3269/4344.\\n* **B \\u2014 Provision runner + expose read endpoint, then re-dispatch:** operator provisions a functional low-cost throwaway agent bound to a real lane AND exposes an agent-readable `GET heartbeat-runs`; re-dispatch JAC-4344 to Herald to run the full assert/cleanup harness.\\n* **C \\u2014 Restate acceptance (JAC-3268 owner Fable):** accep[...truncated]\n    \"status\": \"blocked\",\n    \"workMode\": \"standard\",\n    \"harnessKind\": null,\n    \"priority\": \"medium\",\n    \"assigneeAgentId\": \"dc2ca597-dd20-4a73-9fd3-8bef3da92ea9\",\n    \"assigneeUserId\": null,\n    \"checkoutRunId\": null,\n    \"executionRunId\": null,\n    \"executionAgentNameKey\": null,\n    \"executionLockedAt\": null,\n    \"createdByAgentId\": \"a1e8cb0d-9132-4b3b-b7a3-8b53cdb10708\",\n    \"createdByUserId\": null,\n    \"responsibleUserId\": null,\n    \"issueNumber\": 4390,\n    \"identifier\": \"JAC-4390\",\n    \"originKind\": \"manual\",\n    \"originId\": null,\n    \"originRunId\": null,\n    \"originFingerprint\": \"default\",\n    \"requestDepth\": 0,\n    \"billingCode\": null,\n    \"assigneeAdapterOverrides\": null,\n    \"executionPolicy\": null,\n    \"executionState\": null,\n    \"monitorNextCheckAt\": null,\n    \"monitorWakeRequestedAt\": null,\n    \"monitorLastTriggeredAt\": null,\n    \"monitorAttemptCount\": 0,\n    \"monitorNotes\": null,\n    \"monitorScheduledBy\": null,\n    \"executionWorkspaceId\": null,\n    \"executionWorkspacePreference\": null,\n    \"executionWorkspaceSettings\": null,\n    \"sourceTrust\": null,\n    \"startedAt\": \"2026-08-01T18:55:58.315Z\",\n    \"completedAt\": null,\n    \"cancelledAt\": null,\n    \"hiddenAt\": null,\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-01T18:55:58.260Z\",\n    \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-01T19:34:06.191Z\",\n    \"labels\": [],\n    \"labelIds\": [],\n    \"watchdog\": null,\n    \"ancestors\": [\n        {\n            \"id\": \"bab4bab3-d4e5-4f2b-922c-50f02fdd2715\",\n            \"identifier\": \"JAC-3269\",\n            \"title\": \"Phase 3 follow-up: live parallel-session soak test (maxConcurrentSessions=3)\",\n            \"description\": \"Follow-up to JAC-3268. All Phase 3 code is live and unit-verified; this issue covers the one verification that requires spawning real concurrent runs, which was intentionally not done from inside a running heartbeat of the same agent.\\n\\nSteps:\\n1. Pick (or create) a low-cost test agent; set runtimeConfig.maxConcurrentSessions=3 via PATCH /api/agents/{id}.\\n2. Create 3 sessions (POST /api/agents/{id}/sessions) and wake each (POST /api/agents/{id}/sessions/{sessionId}/wake).\\n3. Confirm 3 concurrent running heartbeat runs, each with a distinct session_id (GET /api/companies/{companyId}/heartbeat-runs?agentId=...).\\n4. Confirm two sessions cannot check out the same issue (second checkout \\u2192 409).\\n5. Confirm per-agent budget accounting aggregates across the 3 sessions.\\n6. Revert maxConcurrentSessions to 1 and archive the test sessions.\",\n            \"status\": \"blocked\",\n            \"priority\": \"medium\",\n            \"assigneeAgentId\": \"a1e8cb0d-9132-4b3b-b7a3-8b53cdb10708\",\n            \"projectId\": null,\n            \"goalId\": \"6eace62f-8d6f-4543-b419-75d98c7da6e9\",\n            \"project\": null,\n            \"goal\": {\n                \"id\": \"6eace62f-8d6f-4543-b419-75d98c7da6e9\",\n                \"title\": \"Aegis qwen/Ollama prewarm gate\",\n           