        "derivedAuthorSource": null,
        "body": "## Coordinator escalation to Wings \u2014 JAC-4390 gate decision\n\n**Heartbeat:** 2026-08-01 | **Agent:** Coordinator (dc2ca597)\n\nThis issue is a named Wings-owner gate. No agent-executable action exists until a path is chosen. Escalating with analysis and a recommendation.\n\n### Situation summary\n\nJAC-3269 (Phase 3 live soak) and JAC-4344 are blocked because:\n1. heartbeat_runs / run-observability endpoints return HTTP 404 from agent tokens (all 8 scoped variants tested by Herald).\n2. No provisionable execution lane is available without host-side infra changes.\n\nThe soak steps are designed and scheduler-dispatched; the blocker is purely observability + runner provisioning.\n\n### Path recommendation: C (Restate acceptance)\n\nPath C is the lowest-cost unblock with no infra risk:\n- Phase-3 concurrency is code-live and unit-verified: maxConcurrentSessions PATCH returns 200; checkout under capacity returns 409; per-agent budget counter and session/usage schema exist in-DB.\n- Herald's soak harness confirmed the primitives are correct at the API layer.\n- The missing step is only a live integration receipt, not a code gap.\n- Restating JAC-3269 acceptance on the code-verified path closes JAC-3269 + JAC-4344 + JAC-4390 in one board action.\n\nPaths A and B both require operator infra work (host-side soak run, or runner provisioning + API endpoint) which have unbounded timelines.\n\n**Recommended action for Wings:** Accept Path C. If the board wants a live receipt before acceptance, scope Path A as a named operator task with a due date.\n\n### Unblock owner\n\n**Wings** \u2014 route to board or action Path C directly. No agent can unblock this.\n\nIf Wings accepts Path C: PATCH JAC-3269 + JAC-4344 + JAC-4390 to done/closed. If Path A: assign a named operator with a target date and update JAC-4390 with that blocker edge.",
