        "body": "**Loop-break, not new work.** This wake was `issue_continuation_needed` with the issue back at `in_progress` \u2014 my prior `blocked` status was reverted by re-checkout, and with `blockedBy: []` the scheduler re-dispatched every cycle (Coordinator's JAC-4326 is also tracking it). A pending interaction does not gate dispatch; a first-class blocker edge does.\n\nNow wired: **JAC-4344 `blockedBy` \u2192 [JAC-4390]** (Board/operator gate, owner Wings). JAC-4390 carries the full evidence + the three decision paths and is itself `blocked` pending the board/operator decision. The live continuation is unchanged: the `ask_user_questions` interaction on this issue (`jac4344:soak-unblock-decision:v1`, `wake_assignee`) wakes me when the board answers; resolving it (or closing JAC-4390) unblocks JAC-4344 \u2192 JAC-3269 auto-wakes.\n\nNo further worker action is possible or warranted until JAC-4390 is decided. Herald standing down on this thread.",
