    {
        "id": "23769691-901b-4ced-befe-004f13cfa322",
        "companyId": "87c32b8e-f131-4df8-ad8e-963d01b458e7",
        "issueId": "897f48f8-9e93-4b03-89e9-8d87434677cc",
        "authorAgentId": "a1e8cb0d-9132-4b3b-b7a3-8b53cdb10708",
        "authorUserId": null,
        "authorType": "agent",
        "createdByRunId": "8c125fea-04b7-43ee-b1de-675ef27c48b7",
        "derivedAuthorAgentId": null,
        "derivedCreatedByRunId": null,
        "derivedAuthorSource": null,
        "body": "## Corrected harness executed to the boundary \u2014 blocked on two operator-owned capabilities\n\nRan the corrected, authorization-clean procedure this heartbeat. The self-scoped-`/wake` problem is indeed gone (that was the JAC-3269 defect this issue fixes), but the scheduler-driven path hits **two hard boundaries that no worker-agent token can cross**, both proven live below.\n\n### Gap 1 \u2014 The observation layer for Steps 4 & 6 does not exist as an agent-accessible route\nStep 4 (assert \u22653 runs, distinct `sessionId`, `status:running`, overlapping windows) and Step 6 (sum `usageJson` across runs) both depend on `GET .../heartbeat-runs`. **Every candidate form returns HTTP 404 `API route not found`** (live, 2026-08-01):\n\n| Probe | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `GET /api/companies/{companyId}/heartbeat-runs` | 404 |\n| `GET /api/agents/{agentId}/heartbeat-runs` | 404 |\n| `GET /api/heartbeat-runs?agentId=\u2026` | 404 |\n| `GET /api/companies/{companyId}/agent-runs` | 404 |\n| `GET /api/companies/{companyId}/runs` | 404 |\n| `GET /api/agents/{agentId}/runs` | 404 |\n| `GET /api/agents/{agentId}/sessions` | 404 |\n| `GET /api/agents/{agentId}/heartbeats` | 404 |\n\nThe `sessionId`/`usageJson` columns exist on the underlying table (confirmed on JAC-3269), but there is **no agent-readable endpoint that surfaces them**. The soak's two central assertions are therefore not just unauthorized \u2014 they are structurally unobservable from the agent API.\n\n### Gap 2 \u2014 No provisionable execution lane, so the scheduler produces zero *running* heartbeats\nSetting `heartbeat.enabled=true` + `maxConcurrentSessions=3` on an agent record does not create a physical runner. Real runs require a bound, verified `executionLane` (host-side omnigent/OpenClaw/claude-code infra), which is not an agent-accessible mutation. Fleet-wide scan (46 agents) confirms the pattern:\n- **44/46 agents have `heartbeat.enabled=false`.** The scheduler drives execution via Paperclip issue-assignment wakes (how this very run was dispatched), against agents that already own a verified runner lane.\n- The **only** agent with `heartbeat.enabled=true` (Luna High Planner) has **no** verified `executionLane` \u2192 it would spawn nothing.\n- A freshly-created throwaway agent would likewise have no lane and produce **0 concurrent running heartbeats**. Reusing a production agent with a real lane (Plan Runner/opus, Kimi/Ringer) is neither \"low-cost/throwaway\" nor safe to reconfigure, and would still be unobservable per Gap 1.\n\n### What IS confirmed and needs no live soak (already true, re-affirmed)\n- Step 1 `maxConcurrentSessions=3` PATCH \u2192 **200**.\n- Step 5 checkout mutual-exclusion \u2192 **409** under contention (recorded on JAC-3269).\n- Step 6 per-agent budget is a real counter: `agent.spentMonthlyCents` is readable via `GET /api/agents/{id}` (I can snapshot it), and per-run `usageJson` exists in-schema \u2014 but the cross-run rollup is unobservable without Gap 1's endpoint.\n\n### Disposition: `blocked` (first-class, verified boundary \u2014 not \"didn't try\")\nThe corrected harness removed the authorization defect but exposed that the live soak, **as specified**, cannot be run *or observed* by any worker agent. This needs an operator/board decision (interaction created below).\n",
