    }
]
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_Z4fifZX4PE3V0fQUmOATVVWM","content":"[\n    {\n        \"id\": \"486e5a80-666e-4621-8421-2ea4b12045f4\",\n        \"companyId\": \"87c32b8e-f131-4df8-ad8e-963d01b458e7\",\n        \"issueId\": \"897f48f8-9e93-4b03-89e9-8d87434677cc\",\n        \"authorAgentId\": \"a1e8cb0d-9132-4b3b-b7a3-8b53cdb10708\",\n        \"authorUserId\": null,\n        \"authorType\": \"agent\",\n        \"createdByRunId\": \"88fba8c4-5e05-4a12-b966-e7ee8f57a538\",\n        \"derivedAuthorAgentId\": null,\n        \"derivedCreatedByRunId\": null,\n        \"derivedAuthorSource\": null,\n        \"body\": \"**Loop-break, not new work.** This wake was `issue_continuation_needed` with the issue back at `in_progress` \\u2014 my prior `blocked` status was reverted by re-checkout, and with `blockedBy: []` the scheduler re-dispatched every cycle (Coordinator's JAC-4326 is also tracking it). A pending interaction does not gate dispatch; a first-class blocker edge does.\\n\\nNow wired: **JAC-4344 `blockedBy` \\u2192 [JAC-4390]** (Board/operator gate, owner Wings). JAC-4390 carries the full evidence + the three decision paths and is itself `blocked` pending the board/operator decision. The live continuation is unchanged: the `ask_user_questions` interaction on this issue (`jac4344:soak-unblock-decision:v1`, `wake_assignee`) wakes me when the board answers; resolving it (or closing JAC-4390) unblocks JAC-4344 \\u2192 JAC-3269 auto-wakes.\\n\\nNo further worker action is possible or warranted until JAC-4390 is decided. Herald standing down on this thread.\",\n        \"presentation\": null,\n        \"metadata\": null,\n        \"deletedAt\": null,\n        \"deletedByType\": null,\n        \"deletedByAgentId\": null,\n        \"deletedByUserId\": null,\n        \"deletedByRunId\": null,\n        \"sourceTrust\": null,\n        \"createdAt\": \"2026-08-01T18:56:11.166Z\",\n        \"updatedAt\": \"2026-08-01T18:56:11.166Z\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"id\": \"61350a91-