    "title": "Rebase fleet patches onto 2026.722.0 + full side-by-side smoke (supersedes 707 integration)",
    "description": "Child of JAC-3662. Board decision (Jack, 2026-08-01): **rebase onto latest stable = `2026.722.0`** (canary `2026.801.0-canary.11` stays out per standing policy). This moves the integration base from 707 \u2192 722, so it effectively re-does the JAC-3664 (707) integration on the new base. **Does NOT authorize the disruptive prod cutover** \u2014 that stays gated in JAC-3666 (needs explicit Jack window approval).\n\n## Progress already landed (this run)\n- Isolated install of `paperclipai@2026.722.0` at `/Users/hermes/.paperclip-smoke-722` (local prefix \u2014 global 626.0 that prod uses is untouched). Version verified `2026.722.0`.\n- Isolated `doctor` runs cleanly (only expected failure: no config in empty `--data-dir`), confirming the 722 CLI is functional. Evidence: `/Users/hermes/.paperclip/upgrade-jac-3662/smoke-722-20260801/doctor-722.txt`.\n- Fresh verified backup already exists (JAC-3662 preflight): `paperclip-jac3662-preflight-20260801-082521.sql.gz`, sha256 `134ab247\u2026d4d4f7`, on-box + Talaris off-box.\n\n## Remaining work\n1. **Onboard an isolated smoke instance** on the 722 install: `--data-dir /Users/hermes/.paperclip-smoke-722/data`, app port **3130**, PG **54349** (3120/3110 historically used; 3120 was the torn-down JAC-3664 canary). Empty/smoke company OR restore the preflight backup into the disposable instance.\n2. `doctor` green; verify adapter registry includes `hermes_local`, `openclaw_gateway`, `pi_local`.\n3. Throwaway agent + one issue run end-to-end.\n4. **Re-integrate fleet patches on 722** (carried from JAC-3664/inventory; re-verify each still needed / not already upstream in 722):\n   - hermes compat `43439143f`\n   - db sessions + rejournal `e56da32b7`\n   - false-green / watchdog `ef019475b` lineage\n   - pause-hold `48e2153f7`\n   - **migration 0125 collision** (local `0125_agent_sessions` vs official `0125_environment_custom_image_templates`) \u2014 must rejournal for the isolated canary; NEVER rewrite prod ledger (JAC-3650).\n   - 722-specific product risks to check: OpenClaw PROTOCOL_VERSION, trimmed issue-detail REST payloads, user-specific runtime secrets/attribution.\n5. Freeze the integration SHA once hermes+db merged onto the 722 canary branch.\n\n## Definition of done\nSide-by-side health proof on 722 + adapter registry confirmed + one green agent run + known-regressions list. Then JAC-3666 (prod cutover) proceeds only on Jack's window approval; JAC-3665 target updated 707\u2192722.",
