    "title": "DECISION (Jack): re-enable ollama-cloud as autonomous tier-2? (JAC-3673 enforcement)",
    "description": "Re-scoped per board request (JAC-3673 comment) to hold **only** enforcement decision #1. Decision #2 (adapter migration) split into its own sibling issue.\n\nEnforcement follow-up to **JAC-3673** (routing policy \u2014 done, ratified). This is a **human authorization call** \u2014 an autonomous agent must not self-authorize it.\n\n## The decision\nRe-enable **ollama-cloud** as the autonomous ladder's **tier-2** (`local \u2192 ollama-cloud \u2192 OpenAI \u2192 Claude`)?\n- Quota restored ~18:59 CDT 2026-07-19, but cloud routes stayed removed (P0 **hermes-qds0**) and re-enabling was **NOT authorized** in the 07-19 session.\n\n## If authorized \u2014 required steps before any config change\n1. **Re-probe live** \u2014 never trust `hermes auth status` (reports \"logged in\" for quota-exhausted/401 creds). Use the disposable-profile method in `docs/provider-liveness-probe-method-2026-07-18.md`.\n2. **Verify the Talaris half of hermes-qds0** \u2014 never verified; stale cloud routes there would silently resume metering the moment quota is live.\n3. Add ollama-cloud to the `local-first` ladder in `scripts/provider_first_profile.py`.\n\nOnce Jack rules \"yes\", any agent can pick this up and execute under explicit authorization.\n\nRefs: JAC-3673 (policy, done), bd memory `paperclip-autonomous-routing-policy`, hermes-qds0.",
