                "id": "f99704da-43b5-4cf7-89ef-13f59a348d90",
                "name": "Agentic OS",
                "description": "## Purpose\nThe coordination and runtime layer for the jack.digital agent fleet. Agentic OS integrates work-state, memory, orchestration, dashboards, and operator-facing control surfaces without collapsing their separate authorities.\n\n## Scope\n- Fleet orchestration, routing, health, and command-centre surfaces\n- Paperclip, Beads, Hermes, and memory-system integration\n- Durable handoffs, evidence receipts, governance, and deployment verification\n- Shared runtime contracts used by downstream projects\n\n## Canonical systems\n- Code: `/Users/hermes/Projects/agentic-os`\n- Git origin: `/Users/hermes/git/agentic-os.git` (local bare repository, not a collaboration URL)\n- Lifecycle work state: Beads and Paperclip according to their declared lanes\n- Governance/federation knowledge: ContextForge pointer layer, not work-state SSOT\n\n## Current state\nActive integration project. Preserve source-of-truth boundaries: Paperclip manages company/project/issue execution; Beads remains durable lifecycle state; ContextForge indexes and disambiguates; Hermes provides the active agent runtime.\n\n## Connections\n- [Onboarding](/projects/60bf492f-74ce-4084-83c9-d80c5f8bfaa9) \u2014 fleet induction\n- [Sea Ranch AI](/projects/3edbceaa-842b-4cbd-8a2d-a06b9264db86), [Echo Springs](/projects/97c2505c-53bb-4975-964f-0a5f6780b419), and [Health](/projects/24790c7e-0ab5-403c-89da-e13b0a460ea7) \u2014 downstream operational domains\n- Paperclip MCP provides operational query/write access. ContextForge MCP provides shared pointer/index access; it does not create native Paperclip project relations.\n\n**Stable project ID:** `f99704da-43b5-4cf7-89ef-13f59a348d90`",
